V="https://youtu.be/CGZXTuUrcXQ"; M="https://youtu.be/qtgfd_s4zBk"
def t(ts):
    p=[int(x) for x in ts.split(":")]
    while len(p)<3: p.insert(0,0)
    return f"{V}?t={p[0]*3600+p[1]*60+p[2]}"
d=Doc("Dalia Dippolito — \"Can I See My Husband?\" (Full Episode Script)",
 "Spec script in the interrogation-channel format. Boynton Beach, Florida, August 5, 2009: a newlywed is told her husband has been murdered, taken to the station as the grieving widow, and then shown the man she thought she had hired.",
 [("Boynton Beach PD interrogation video of Dalia Dippolito, Aug 5, 2009 (31 min). Timestamps and links below refer to this file.",V),
  ("Boynton Beach PD interview of Michael Dippolito, Aug 5, 2009, 7:19 a.m. (20 min). Timestamps for this file to be set at the edit.",M),
  ("Police video of the staged scene outside the townhouse, Aug 5, 2009, as broadcast on Cops (for the setup)","https://youtu.be/Pp4zAxP27Uw"),
  ("Undercover recording of Aug 3, 2009, CVS parking lot (public; the \"5,000 percent\" exchange)","")],
 "Every transcription line is taken from the released recordings; the interrogation lines were cleaned from the video's caption track and must be checked against the audio at the edit. No dialogue has been reconstructed.")
d.h("INTRO")
d.ed("open on the Cops footage of the taped-off townhouse, morning light, sirens off. Audio first, then picture.")
d.clip("Interrogation","0:00:11-0:00:23",url=t("0:00:11"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: First of all, let me just tell you I'm sorry for your loss.","Dalia: I just want to see my husband, please.","Sergeant: No, you don't want to see him. Believe me, you don't."])
d.clip("Michael Dippolito interview","set at edit")
d.tr(["Michael: It's like a bad movie, you know. It really doesn't surprise me at all."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:15:05-0:15:20",url=t("0:15:05"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: You need a real good attorney, because we're going to show him the film where you say you're 5,000 percent sure you want him dead. You think I made that up?"])
d.ed("hard cut to black on \"made that up\". Title card.")
d.h("SET UP")
d.nar("Dalia and Michael Dippolito had been married six months. He was 38, on probation for a fraud conviction, and trying to buy his way off it. She was 26. In July 2009, a man Dalia had been seeing on the side walked into the Boynton Beach police department and said she had asked him to find her a hitman. Before any of that, there was the question of how the two of them had met. Michael answered it himself, at 7:19 that morning.")
d.clip("Michael Dippolito interview","set at edit")
d.tr(["Michael: We met, I believe, in October, and she's actually an escort. That's how I met her. She came to my office one day."])
d.ed("show the probable-cause affidavit cover and the line about the $1,200 for a gun. No photos of the informant.")
d.nar("Police gave her a hitman. On August 3rd an undercover officer, Widy Jean, met her in a CVS parking lot with a camera running. He asked if she was sure. Her answer is the reason this case has a name. She said she was five thousand percent sure. Then she gave him a key to the house, and a time: Wednesday morning, when she would be at the gym.")
d.clip("Cops staged-scene footage","set at edit","officers stringing crime scene tape across the front door; no audio under the narration")
d.nar("On Wednesday morning she went to the gym. While she was gone, Boynton Beach police taped off her front door, parked their cars in the street, and invited a camera crew from the television show Cops to film what happened next. Her husband, who had had back surgery the week before, was already with detectives. Then they called her and asked her to come home. A sergeant met her in the street and told her Michael was dead. She collapsed. They put her in a car and drove her to the station, as a widow.")
d.ed("Cops footage: Dalia arriving, the sergeant telling her, her reaction. Keep it under fifteen seconds. We are not going to replay the scream.")
d.h("INTERVIEW START")
d.clip("Interrogation","0:00:27-0:01:30","Miranda, read to a woman who thinks she is a victim",url=t("0:00:27"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: I'm required to warn you before you make any statement that you have the following constitutional rights. And as I said, this is protocol… You have the right to remain silent and not answer any questions. Do you understand that?","Dalia: Yes."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:02:33-0:03:05",url=t("0:02:33"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: Okay, listen. Is there anybody that you know that you think would want to kill your husband?","Dalia: My husband's on probation for… stock fraud.","Sergeant: How long has he been on probation?","Dalia: Two years in prison and five years on probation, going on to six years."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:03:24-0:04:00",url=t("0:03:24"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: Is there anybody you could think of that would want to do this to him?","Dalia: He's been trying to get off probation and it's just been nothing but problems the whole time… People weren't happy that he was getting off probation, because it's a lot of money he's got to pay back."])
d.nar("For ten minutes she gives the detectives a suspect list. Men from his old fraud case. A man they ran into at Target a few days ago. Organized crime. She mentions the $191,000 he owed in restitution, and that the money had gone missing. The sergeant writes it all down. He already knows the money went missing. He has spent two days listening to her explain where.")
d.clip("Interrogation","0:07:18-0:07:30",url=t("0:07:18"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: You're lucky you went to the gym.","Dalia: We were supposed to go to the gym.","Sergeant: Both of you were supposed to go?","Dalia: He didn't know if he was going to. He just had liposuction."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:08:38-0:09:20",url=t("0:08:38"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: I don't know if you know, he was shot. He was shot twice… Evidently your husband answered the door and they took him back upstairs, in your bedroom.","Dalia: Why would he answer the door? He doesn't answer for anybody he doesn't know."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:09:27-0:09:40",url=t("0:09:27"))
d.tr(["Dalia: We have cameras. The front door has camera, back door has cameras, but they don't record. Nobody knows, but they don't record."])
d.ed("freeze on \"nobody knows\" for one second.")
d.nar("That is the sentence the detectives were waiting for. The cameras do not record. Nobody knows. The hitman had been told the same thing in the parking lot. The sergeant stands up, says he needs to call the scene, and leaves her alone for ninety seconds. When he comes back, he is not asking questions anymore.")
d.clip("Interrogation","0:12:55-0:13:26",url=t("0:12:55"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: Now, you know that I advised you of your rights, right?","Dalia: Yes.","Sergeant: Okay. The game's over with. Okay? There's no more games with you and I. Now we're going to get down to serious business. I want to know if you know this guy. Come here. Bring this guy in here.","Sergeant: You know who this guy is?","Dalia: No. I've never seen him before."])
d.ed("the man brought in is the undercover officer, in handcuffs, as if under arrest. Freeze on her face, not his.")
d.clip("Interrogation","0:13:46-0:14:49",url=t("0:13:46"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: You're going to jail today for solicitation of murder. You're under arrest. That's an undercover police officer. We filmed everything that you did, recorded everything that you did.","Dalia: I didn't do anything.","Sergeant: Everything has been recorded. You were photographed in the convertible when you sat in his car in front of CVS.","Dalia: I didn't do anything. Please.","Sergeant: Your husband is well and alive.","Dalia: Thank God.","Sergeant: Oh yeah, thank God.","Dalia: Can I see him?","Sergeant: No. He doesn't want to see you."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:15:05-0:15:40",url=t("0:15:05"))
d.tr(["Sergeant: You need a real good attorney, because we're going to show him the film where you say you're 5,000 percent sure you want him dead. You think I made that up?… When I leave this room, no other officer will ever talk to you again. Next time we see you is when you're in trial."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:16:48-0:17:03","Michael appears in the doorway",url=t("0:16:48"))
d.tr(["Dalia: Come here, please. Come here, Mike. Come here.","Dalia: I didn't do anything!"])
d.nar("Michael Dippolito had been in the building for an hour. At 7:19 that morning, while his wife was still being treated as a widow down the hall, two detectives sat him down and asked him to start from the beginning.")
d.clip("Michael Dippolito interview","set at edit")
d.tr(["Michael: I basically, I lost $240,000 with this girl. It's unexplainable money. Just stupid stories, one after the other. I'm the stupid one, you know."])
d.clip("Michael Dippolito interview","set at edit")
d.tr(["Michael: I had drugs planted on my truck. The officers came out to search my truck. I'm not a drug dealer, and I never was.","Michael: One day I come out of the gym, there's a note on my car: we need $40,000 in a bag, don't tell your wife."])
d.nar("Twice in seven months, police had searched his truck after anonymous tips, and twice found small amounts of drugs that he says were not his. Each time, the only person who knew where the truck was parked was his wife. He had lost two friends who told him something was wrong. His mother had stopped talking about it. He had kept giving her the benefit of the doubt right up to that morning, when she said she was going to the gym and would bring him a coffee.")
d.clip("Michael Dippolito interview","set at edit")
d.tr(["Detective: Now that you've found this out about your wife, how do you feel?","Michael: Whatever she gets, she deserves. I mean, I'll do whatever I have to do to help this case move along.","Detective: I'm sorry about everything, but your life was saved today.","Michael: Honestly, I'm not even grasping that yet."])
d.nar("Back in the other room, a new detective takes over. Alex Moreno has been running the case since the informant walked in. He reads her rights a second time, because the first time she was listening as a victim.")
d.clip("Interrogation","0:23:13-0:24:20",url=t("0:23:13"))
d.tr(["Moreno: Do you understand what happened today? What's going on here?","Dalia: A little.","Moreno: You're being arrested for soliciting to commit murder. What that means is you attempted to hire someone to kill somebody else. Meaning your husband.","Dalia: No. I never done that."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:25:35-0:26:08",url=t("0:25:35"))
d.tr(["Dalia: I'm gonna talk to my husband.","Moreno: Well, you can't talk to your husband. He's not here right now. We let him go home. He's taking care of the house and the dog. So obviously your husband's alive. You saw him, right?","Dalia: I saw him. I'd like to talk to him.","Moreno: And did you see that black officer that was here in handcuffs? Well, he's an officer. So does it get any clearer than that?"])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:27:45-0:28:25",url=t("0:27:45"))
d.tr(["Dalia: I'd like to make a phone call. I just feel lost… Everyone keeps coming and I'm signing all these things and going over all these things, and I don't really know what they're for."])
d.clip("Interrogation","0:30:19-0:30:50",url=t("0:30:19"))
d.tr(["Detective: You sound like a fool right now, denying this. Like my partner just said, everything's on tape. Video and audio.","Dalia: I want to go home.","Detective: You're not going home. You're being arrested.","Dalia: So what do I have to do to go home?","Detective: You can't. It's impossible. You're going to the Palm Beach County Jail after this."])
d.ed("end the interview section on \"what do I have to do to go home\". Fade to black before the detective's answer finishes.")
d.h("OUTRO")
d.nar("In 2011 a jury convicted Dalia Dippolito of solicitation to commit first-degree murder and she was sentenced to 20 years. An appeals court threw that out over errors in jury selection. Her second trial, in 2016, ended with the jury split three to three. Her defense by then was that the whole thing had been an act: a reality-show stunt that the police, and the cameras, had been happy to play along with. Michael Dippolito and the informant both denied it under oath.")
d.nar("In June 2017 a third jury took ninety minutes to convict her. On July 21st, 2017, she was sentenced to 16 years in prison. Nobody was hurt in this case. That is the strangest thing about it, and the reason the footage still exists: for one morning, the only person in Boynton Beach who believed a man had been murdered was the woman who had paid for it.")
d.ed("end on the Cops exterior shot, tape still up, no people in frame.")
d.notes(["Checked against the RTC writing guide: every narration break is under 60 seconds, no clip run between narration breaks is over three minutes, and the set up is broken up by Michael's own line and the Cops footage.",
 "Writer's share (narration plus intro and set-up transcriptions) is about 800 words, inside the 700-1,500 range; the interview transcriptions are included as a courtesy for the transcription team.",
 "YouTube safety: no reenactment of the scream, no replay of the staged-scene reaction beyond fifteen seconds, the informant is not named, the escort detail is Michael's own words and stays in his clip.",
 "Interrogation lines were cleaned from the video's auto-captions; a final pass against the audio is required before the cut. Michael's interview has no caption track yet, so those clips carry no timestamp.",
 "The Aug 3 parking-lot recording is public but not in the source files; the \"5,000 percent\" line is used only as the sergeant quotes it."])
